MonoGame for MSYS2 (CLANG64, .NET 8 bootstrap SDK)
===================================================

Everything here is built from source. No MonoGame.Library.* / MonoGame.Tool.*
native packages, no SharpDX and no precompiled effects from upstream are used.

Installed
---------
- lib/dotnet/library-packs: MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL,
  MonoGame.Framework.Content.Pipeline, MonoGame.Content.Builder.Task and the
  dotnet-mgcb / dotnet-mgfxc tool packages (offline NuGet feed of the SDK).
- lib/dotnet/templates/8.0.131: MonoGame.Templates.CSharp, so
  `dotnet new mgdesktopgl -o MyGame` works without `dotnet new install`.
- lib/monogame/{mgcb,mgfxc}: the content builder and effect compiler,
  with `mgcb` and `mgfxc` wrappers in bin/.

Creating a game
---------------
    dotnet new mgdesktopgl -o MyGame
    cd MyGame && dotnet build && dotnet run

MonoGame.Content.Builder.Task uses lib/monogame/mgcb/mgcb.dll instead of
restoring the dotnet-mgcb tool from nuget.org (set MGCBCommand to override).
The template's .config/dotnet-tools.json only lists dotnet-mgcb; the
mgcb-editor tools are not built.

Native libraries
----------------
- DesktopGL games copy SDL2.dll and libopenal-1.dll (and the MSYS2 DLLs they
  link, e.g. libc++.dll) from $MINGW_PREFIX/bin into the output directory
  (MonoGameCopyNativeLibraries=false to disable, MonoGameNativeLibraryDir to
  take them from elsewhere). At runtime a DLL next to the game wins, then the
  MSYS2 prefix of the running .NET runtime.
- mgfxc and the content pipeline compile HLSL with the vkd3d-based
  d3dcompiler_47.dll from mingw-w64-clang-x86_64-vkd3d-d3dcompiler
  ($MINGW_PREFIX/lib/vkd3d-d3dcompiler, never System32; MGFXC_D3DCOMPILER
  overrides the path) and translate to GLSL with libmojoshader.dll
  (monogame-mojoshader). Fonts use libfreetype-6.dll, models use Assimp
  (dotnet-assimpnetter on mingw-w64-assimp), textures use mgpipeline.dll built
  here with stb from the MSYS2 stb package. Audio/video content runs
  ffmpeg/ffprobe from the MSYS2 ffmpeg package (optional dependency).

Not available
-------------
- crunch (DXT3, ETC1, ETC2A texture compression) and basisu (ASTC, PVRTC,
  ATC, BC7 and other mobile formats) have no MSYS2 packages; those texture
  formats fail with a "not found" error unless crunch.exe / basisu.exe are on
  PATH. DXT1/DXT5 ("Compressed" on DesktopGL) use the managed BCnEncoder.
- dxc (DirectX 12 and Vulkan shader profiles) is not packaged. The OpenGL and
  DirectX_11 profiles work.
- The MGCB editor (mgcb-editor, Eto.Forms) is not built.

Shaders
-------
On the OpenGL profile mgfxc does not carry HLSL initializers (`float x = 1;`)
into the effect (upstream MonoGame behaviour: MojoShader exposes no default
values); set such parameters from code. DirectX_11 output has no "Aon9"
(feature level 9) chunk, as vkd3d does not emit one.

The stock effects embedded in MonoGame.Framework.dll are compiled from their
.fx sources during the build. vkd3d's shader model 2 register allocator needs
13 temporaries for several SkinnedEffect vertex shaders (vs_2_0 allows 12),
so SkinnedEffect's vertex shaders are compiled as vs_3_0 for OpenGL. Custom
effects that fit vs_2_0/ps_2_0 with fxc may need vs_3_0/ps_3_0 here for the
same reason.
